# ============================================================
# NOTES, SPECS AND PLANNING DOCS — NEVER COMMIT
# ============================================================
# netlify.toml sets publish = "." so EVERY committed file ships
# to the CDN and is fetchable over HTTP. A _redirects rule can
# shadow a path, but the file is still deployed and the shadow
# is one line deep — on 2026-08-22 a whole-file upload wiped the
# /netlify/* block and exposed the function source for an hour.
#
# So markdown and internal docs are kept OUT OF THE REPO, not
# hidden inside it. They live in the parent project folder
# (../), which git cannot see.
#
# If a .md ever genuinely has to ship, unignore it explicitly
# with a ! rule and add a redirect only if it must stay private.
# ============================================================
*.md
docs/
